From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:39:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] drm/msm: iceland: built-in defaults for the board's
 command line switches

The OnePlus Pad 4 boots with a long list of msm switches on its kernel
command line. Most of them already equal the driver defaults; four do
not: msm.dpu_dsc_once=1, msm.dpu_idle_refresh_ms=1000,
msm.dpu_idle_refresh_hz=30, and - with the vendor GPU firmware pair only -
msm.enable_preemption=1 and msm.enable_clx=1.

Add CONFIG_DRM_MSM_ICELAND_DEFAULTS. Those switches now remember an
explicit value (command line or sysfs). On the board whose root
compatible is "oneplus,iceland", and only there, the driver applies the
board's value to every one of them that was not set: the display values
before the encoders are created, the GPU values before the ring count is
chosen. Preemption and CLX are proven only with the vendor GMU v5.3.33 /
SQE 0x094 pair (preemption with the stock or linux-firmware pair reset
the board early in boot), so they default on only when the GMU and SQE
files the firmware loader finds have that pair's sha256. Other boards
and an explicit value are not affected.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
